1
00:00:01,039 --> 00:00:05,177
Part 2: a live walkthrough of Shaddai, recorded on the demo fixture.

2
00:00:07,582 --> 00:00:13,619
Paste any BSC address. Shaddai reads the raw balances, then the multiplier your wallet ignores.

3
00:00:14,919 --> 00:00:21,681
The landing reads the live multiplier index: the latest changes, and what 100 tokens are in shares.

4
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:34,624
The demo address: NVDAB in the wallet, in Venus and lent on Lista, plus AAPLB, MSFTB, NVDAon and more.

5
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:44,810
Raw is what balanceOf() returns: 10.000000. The multiplier is 1.0017×.

6
00:00:46,598 --> 00:00:53,488
So the address owns 10.017 NVIDIA share-equivalents. Shaddai always shows both numbers.

7
00:00:56,396 --> 00:01:04,652
XMPLB, a fictional demo stock, split 2-for-1: 30 raw tokens on Lista are 60.24 shares.

8
00:01:07,946 --> 00:01:15,263
The ledger: every multiplier change, with no Transfer event behind any of them. Dividends, a split, one pending.

9
00:01:18,959 --> 00:01:24,932
“Did I get the dividend?” One plain answer: when, the raw it applied to, old → new, and shares gained.

10
00:01:27,772 --> 00:01:31,718
When nothing touched the holder, it says so. It never invents a dividend.

11
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:41,475
Each row: raw held at the block before, old → new multiplier, Δ share-equivalents and an estimated USD value.

12
00:01:46,289 --> 00:01:57,809
Every NVIDIA wrapper, priced per share. NVDAB’s raw gap is +0.17%: that is the dividend factor. After the multiplier, 0.00%.

13
00:01:59,599 --> 00:02:11,460
NVDAon’s pool is thin, under $25k, so NVDAB is the tightest liquid wrapper. Outside US hours, rows say: quote, not a mispricing.

14
00:02:16,735 --> 00:02:20,425
Size the buy in dollars of stock: $50 of NVIDIA.

15
00:02:24,306 --> 00:02:33,223
The thin twin is refused before it is quoted: “NVDAon book is $14k, under the $25k floor.”

16
00:02:35,010 --> 00:02:40,492
NVDAB is quoted in share-equivalents and preselected: the most stock for the money.

17
00:02:45,773 --> 00:02:52,834
Step one is an exact-amount approve, decoded and dry-run before a wallet sees it. In the demo nothing is signed.

18
00:02:58,174 --> 00:03:05,960
Lista counts raw tokens, not shares. MSFTB is posted as collateral, with a multiplier change scheduled.

19
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:16,625
Three numbers before the flip: the protocol holds 3 raw, 3.000000 shares today, 3.006060 after.

20
00:03:18,403 --> 00:03:24,163
Plus what a share-priced oracle would do to the collateral value. Confirm the oracle before you borrow.

21
00:03:27,055 --> 00:03:33,199
Nothing scheduled for NVDAB in Venus, so it says so, instead of showing a made-up preview.

22
00:03:38,230 --> 00:03:44,480
One click exports the ledger to CSV, the rows a tax tool reading only transfers would never see.

23
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:52,135
Agents get the same answers as MCP tools. This is sharetrue.dividend, called on the running server.

24
00:03:53,745 --> 00:03:56,667
Your wallet counts tokens. Shaddai counts shares.
